WEBVTT

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:15.820
It is for the best.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:18.420
Until this war is over, you'll be safer on Earth.

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.500
This attorney takes three years.

00:00:21.059 --> 00:00:22.120
It's the only way.

00:00:22.519 --> 00:00:24.320
The council destroyed all the remaining portals.

00:00:24.820 --> 00:00:26.600
The General Zod and his men couldn't escape.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.160
What if I never see you again?

00:00:29.879 --> 00:00:34.960
I'm your father, Kara.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:36.000
Trust my wisdom.

00:00:37.359 --> 00:00:39.780
Everything and everyone that I love is to hear on Krypton.

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:44.000
This crystal is your way back to us.

00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:47.920
As long as you have it, the world you know in love will be safe.

00:00:48.759 --> 00:00:50.119
Why can't you come with me?

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:51.859
I'm needed here to protect Kandah.

00:00:52.159 --> 00:00:53.280
You must protect the crystal.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:55.780
It contains instructions for what you must do

00:00:55.780 --> 00:00:57.060
when you rescue your cousin, Kelle.

00:00:57.899 --> 00:00:59.020
I don't want to go.

00:00:59.579 --> 00:01:02.859
Remember, Kara, the true Kryptonian embraces their destiny

00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:03.579
no matter what.

00:01:04.079 --> 00:01:11.349
I love you.

00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:31.939
I love you, Kara.

00:01:32.480 --> 00:03:02.759
You're infected.

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:04.300
This is what was so urgent.

00:03:04.539 --> 00:03:07.000
Right now, my worries should be the least of your worries, Clark.

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:10.340
The FAA halted all air traffic over Washington late last night.

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.259
Some commercial airline pilot reported a near mist

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:16.000
with an object that shot into the sky in a red-blue blur.

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:17.020
No.

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.020
Yeah.

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.020
Now, they think it may have been a ground-to-air missile,

00:03:20.020 --> 00:03:22.020
but if you ask me, I think we just found...

00:03:22.020 --> 00:03:23.020
Kara.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.020
Chloe, this is all my fault.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:28.020
Clerk, you're not the one who played chicken with an airplane.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:31.020
Thanks. Besides, she's not your responsibility.

00:03:31.020 --> 00:03:33.020
You're her cousin, not her father.

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:35.020
But I pushed her away, Chloe. I didn't trust her.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:36.020
And now she's alone and angry.

00:03:36.020 --> 00:03:39.020
I have to find her and bring her back before she heard someone.

00:03:39.020 --> 00:03:40.020
Or uncorks the Kent family secret.

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:43.020
I mean, clearly, Kara does not fly below the radar.

00:03:43.020 --> 00:03:45.020
Hey, Clark!

00:03:45.020 --> 00:03:47.560
Clark, you hear from Kara, and is she okay?

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:54.099
You guys look worried. What's going on?

00:03:56.219 --> 00:04:00.419
Apparently, Kara decided to go to Washington, D.C., alone, and not tell anyone.

00:04:01.099 --> 00:04:02.319
Maybe she's doing the tourist thing.

00:04:02.919 --> 00:04:03.979
Postcards are probably already in the mail.

00:04:06.900 --> 00:04:08.199
You know something, don't you?

00:04:09.439 --> 00:04:10.639
Jimmy, she's my cousin.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.240
She's my family. If you know anything, you need to tell me.

00:04:17.240 --> 00:04:20.800
Kara asked to see a video that Lois took a so-called spaceship out in Granville.

00:04:21.519 --> 00:04:24.240
The recording was ruined, but I managed to get a partial image of equipment

00:04:24.240 --> 00:04:27.759
that pointed to the government.

00:04:29.980 --> 00:04:32.399
And you didn't tell us this because...

00:04:32.399 --> 00:04:33.939
Because Kara asked me to keep it a secret.

00:04:35.439 --> 00:04:36.480
She trusted me.

00:04:41.319 --> 00:04:43.139
I'm sorry, C.K., she said it was a hobby.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:45.220
I had no idea that she'd follow the lead all the way to Capitol Hill.

00:04:46.439 --> 00:04:47.079
Thanks, Jimmy.

00:04:47.399 --> 00:04:47.639
Chloe.

00:04:48.759 --> 00:04:51.680
If he's right, the government might have Kara's Crystal.

00:04:52.459 --> 00:04:53.839
That's her last tie to Krypton.

00:04:53.959 --> 00:04:55.439
She'll do anything to get it back.

00:05:10.189 --> 00:05:10.829
Welcome back.

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:11.730
Clark.

00:05:12.129 --> 00:05:17.120
I'm glad you're okay.

00:05:18.620 --> 00:05:19.500
Yes, well.

00:05:19.899 --> 00:05:22.899
In the darkest hour, the soul is replenished

00:05:22.899 --> 00:05:26.899
and given strength to continue and endure.

00:05:26.899 --> 00:05:32.620
Luther's are survivors, Clark.

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:36.620
I hear that a new member of the Kent family has turned up in Smallville.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.620
My cousin, Kara.

00:05:38.620 --> 00:05:39.620
Kara.

00:05:39.620 --> 00:05:43.730
You haven't mentioned her before, have you?

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.730
Which side of the family?

00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:46.730
My father's side.

00:05:46.730 --> 00:05:47.730
Oh.

00:05:47.730 --> 00:05:49.730
Which father?

00:05:49.730 --> 00:05:53.839
My adoptive father.

00:05:53.839 --> 00:05:57.120
Look, the reason I'm here,

00:05:57.120 --> 00:06:00.519
I came across an underground government government.

00:06:00.519 --> 00:06:03.519
It's located beneath the silo in Granville.

00:06:03.519 --> 00:06:06.519
You have a lot of contacts in Washington.

00:06:06.519 --> 00:06:08.519
I thought maybe you could tell me something about it.

00:06:08.519 --> 00:06:11.519
What were you doing in a government lab, Clark?

00:06:11.519 --> 00:06:14.519
Researching a story for a friend.

00:06:14.519 --> 00:06:20.899
I believe that lab in Granville belongs to the Department of Domestic Security.

00:06:20.899 --> 00:06:22.899
Tell your friend.

00:06:22.899 --> 00:06:24.899
Tell her it's not a front page story.

00:06:24.899 --> 00:06:25.899
Domestic security.

00:06:25.899 --> 00:06:27.899
I thought they dealt with terrorism.

00:06:27.899 --> 00:06:30.899
Among other things.

00:06:30.899 --> 00:06:31.899
You know, Washington.

00:06:31.899 --> 00:06:34.899
has had a wary eye on the heavens for decades, Clark,

00:06:34.899 --> 00:06:37.899
watching for any threat from beyond the stars.

00:06:37.899 --> 00:06:40.899
I've heard they call that program Star Hawk.

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:44.899
They came to Smallville right after the second meteor shower.

00:06:44.899 --> 00:06:48.899
I've done everything I could to divert their attention away from you.

00:06:48.899 --> 00:06:52.629
Why didn't you say anything to me?

00:06:52.629 --> 00:06:57.449
Your life is complicated enough.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:00.449
I understood they were about to leave Smallville.

00:07:00.449 --> 00:07:04.449
They'd found no conclusive evidence of an alien threat.

00:07:04.449 --> 00:07:14.060
Do you think that something they discovered, something in that lab, changed their minds?

00:07:14.060 --> 00:07:22.120
Tell me everything you know about Star-Hawk.

00:07:22.120 --> 00:07:25.120
Initiated, L-I-E-S.

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:29.459
Spectroscopic analysis almost complete.

00:07:29.459 --> 00:07:38.699
B-S-S-S-S-s-S-s-s-s-s-short pulse.

00:07:38.699 --> 00:07:40.699
Composition.

00:07:40.699 --> 00:07:42.699
Merillium.

00:07:42.699 --> 00:07:44.699
Aluminum silicate with fluorine.

00:07:44.699 --> 00:07:49.980
7% material unknown.

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:51.980
Lock it down.

00:07:51.980 --> 00:07:52.980
Give me a full.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:08:04.069
report as soon as possible.

00:08:04.069 --> 00:08:12.410
Mr. Carter, Mr. Luther has entered the building.

00:08:12.410 --> 00:08:15.410
Quite the brain trust you have here, Agent Carter.

00:08:15.410 --> 00:08:18.410
This is a restricted facility.

00:08:18.410 --> 00:08:21.410
You never told me you stole something from that spacecraft.

00:08:21.410 --> 00:08:23.410
Our work is classified.

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:25.410
For reasons of national security, Mr. Luther.

00:08:25.410 --> 00:08:28.410
And you've obviously made an effort to see it remain secure.

00:08:28.410 --> 00:08:34.409
However, the term classified has never prevented me from getting what I want.

00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:35.409
That's right.

00:08:35.409 --> 00:08:36.409
You've got this angelic.

00:08:36.409 --> 00:08:40.409
Angelic blonde saint watching over you.

00:08:40.409 --> 00:08:49.000
In the halls of power, you don't amount to much, agent.

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:53.000
It's only a matter of time before I find out what it is you're hiding.

00:08:53.000 --> 00:09:13.080
Re-initiating sequence.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:16.080
Yes, sir. Unlocking containment ceiling.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:26.470
Reinitiating L-I-V-S.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:36.070
Laser and X-ray photo electrons spectrographicographic analysis.

00:09:36.070 --> 00:10:00.370
Starting external scan.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.370
I'd rather be out in the field chasing you.

00:10:02.370 --> 00:10:06.370
out in the field chasing you a foes and stuck in a lap.

00:10:06.370 --> 00:10:07.370
I press buttons.

00:10:07.370 --> 00:10:08.370
I'll get samples.

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.370
Half of stuff's hazardous.

00:10:10.370 --> 00:10:11.370
That's what I'm trying to say.

00:10:11.370 --> 00:10:14.370
I've been working so hard I haven't been able to get a date.

00:10:14.370 --> 00:10:16.370
Nice choker.

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:24.679
You, uh, work for domestic security?

00:10:24.679 --> 00:10:29.679
I know I've had a few, but, uh, am I really that office?

00:10:29.679 --> 00:10:31.679
You know what's sexy?

00:10:31.679 --> 00:10:33.679
I thought of a government agent keeping me safe?

00:10:33.679 --> 00:10:35.679
I'm not really an agent.

00:10:35.679 --> 00:10:36.679
Don't tell me you're just one.

00:10:36.679 --> 00:10:38.679
You don't tell me you're just another pencil pusher

00:10:38.679 --> 00:10:40.679
from the home office across the street.

00:10:40.679 --> 00:10:43.679
No, I know, I had up a team of lab technicians outside the city.

00:10:43.679 --> 00:10:45.679
Hmm.

00:10:45.679 --> 00:10:48.679
But we go out in the field a lot.

00:10:48.679 --> 00:10:50.679
Good.

00:10:50.679 --> 00:10:52.679
I was hoping you were hands-on.

00:10:52.679 --> 00:10:53.679
Yeah.

00:10:53.679 --> 00:10:57.679
Ever investigate anything, I don't know, extraterrestrial?

00:10:57.679 --> 00:10:59.679
Excuse me?

00:10:59.679 --> 00:11:05.679
You know, UFOs, aliens, galaxies far, far away.

00:11:05.679 --> 00:11:10.679
I can't really be talking about what I do.

00:11:10.679 --> 00:11:12.679
Life and other planets.

00:11:12.679 --> 00:11:14.679
That's hot.

00:11:14.679 --> 00:11:17.679
I would have loved to have chatted about it.

00:11:17.679 --> 00:11:24.159
Wait.

00:11:24.159 --> 00:11:31.559
So where'd you find the ship?

00:11:31.559 --> 00:11:34.559
Um, Kansas, out in the boondock somewhere.

00:11:34.559 --> 00:11:37.559
Can't believe you work with real flying saucers?

00:11:37.559 --> 00:11:38.559
Yeah.

00:11:38.559 --> 00:11:40.559
That's such a turn on.

00:11:40.559 --> 00:11:43.559
What do you say?

00:11:43.559 --> 00:11:45.559
We get out of here.

00:11:45.559 --> 00:11:46.559
In these spaceships.

00:11:46.559 --> 00:11:48.559
Ever find anything in them?

00:11:48.559 --> 00:11:50.559
We can talk more of my apartment.

00:11:50.559 --> 00:11:51.559
It's not too far away.

00:11:51.559 --> 00:11:54.559
Oh, come on, secret agent man.

00:11:54.559 --> 00:11:59.559
Tell me what was in that ship, and I'll go wherever you want.

00:11:59.559 --> 00:12:02.840
It's just some weird, Crystal.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:04.840
We're studying it at the lab.

00:12:04.840 --> 00:12:09.309
Seriously.

00:12:09.309 --> 00:12:12.309
Do you really think that I can wait till we get to your place?

00:12:12.309 --> 00:12:14.309
Hmm?

00:12:14.309 --> 00:12:15.309
Oh, wow.

00:12:15.309 --> 00:12:17.309
Why do we get a bit more comfortable?

00:12:17.309 --> 00:12:22.799
Hey, where's you?

00:12:22.799 --> 00:13:12.210
Where'd you?

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:13.210
Can I help you?

00:13:13.210 --> 00:13:15.210
Yeah, I was hoping I could get a...

00:13:15.210 --> 00:13:18.519
Chloe.

00:13:18.519 --> 00:13:21.309
Lana.

00:13:21.309 --> 00:13:22.309
What are you doing here?

00:13:22.309 --> 00:13:27.480
I stumbled across the ISIS Foundation website

00:13:27.480 --> 00:13:30.480
and saw they were reaching out to media victims.

00:13:30.480 --> 00:13:34.480
I wanted to see if I could get an interview.

00:13:34.480 --> 00:13:36.480
Do you work here?

00:13:36.480 --> 00:13:37.480
You could say that.

00:13:37.480 --> 00:13:44.610
I actually kind of am the foundation.

00:13:44.610 --> 00:13:49.889
When did Shree come such a champion for the Meteor challenge?

00:13:49.889 --> 00:13:51.889
Lex ruin lives with 33.1, not just...

00:13:51.889 --> 00:13:55.889
not just his victims, but their families and friends.

00:13:55.889 --> 00:13:58.889
I'm using the divorce settlement to fight back.

00:13:58.889 --> 00:14:04.580
This is a little more impressive than just writing a check.

00:14:04.580 --> 00:14:06.580
I mean, this is a major operation.

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:08.580
Right now, it's just me in an office.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.580
But eventually, I'd like to open a free clinic,

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.580
start support group, set up a crisis hotline.

00:14:14.580 --> 00:14:19.009
I'm so proud of you.

00:14:19.009 --> 00:14:21.009
Why didn't you tell me?

00:14:21.009 --> 00:14:25.009
I don't want anyone to know until I've had the chance to build this into something real.

00:14:25.009 --> 00:14:26.009
You're on the web.

00:14:26.009 --> 00:14:27.009
You're on the web.

00:14:27.009 --> 00:14:29.009
You're already out there.

00:14:29.009 --> 00:14:32.009
I launched the site so the people that need to help could find me.

00:14:32.009 --> 00:14:35.009
Grassroots is really all I want right now.

00:14:35.009 --> 00:14:40.009
Chloe, do me a favor and don't tell Clark, okay?

00:14:40.009 --> 00:14:45.009
I thought you two were all about full disclosure now.

00:14:45.009 --> 00:14:46.009
Well, you know how he is.

00:14:46.009 --> 00:14:48.009
He's going to think that the work's too dangerous,

00:14:48.009 --> 00:14:50.009
and he's going to try and talk me out of it.

00:14:50.009 --> 00:14:57.340
Lana, I've interviewed enough people to know when someone's bending the truth.

00:14:57.340 --> 00:14:59.340
And as much as I love what you're doing,

00:14:59.340 --> 00:15:04.649
you're doing, sensing a right angle in here somewhere.

00:15:04.649 --> 00:15:07.649
That right angle is your imagination.

00:15:07.649 --> 00:15:11.649
Please, Chloe, don't tell Clark anything.

00:15:11.649 --> 00:15:18.299
This conversation is officially off the record.

00:15:18.299 --> 00:15:31.750
Give me back my wallet.

00:15:31.750 --> 00:15:34.750
I will want to tell me the relocation of the crystal.

00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.210
Who are you?

00:15:38.210 --> 00:15:39.210
It wasn't in the lab.

00:15:39.210 --> 00:15:40.210
Where is it?

00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:42.210
It's there. We never move it.

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:47.190
Let him go, Kara.

00:15:47.190 --> 00:15:48.190
Give him his wallet back.

00:15:48.190 --> 00:15:59.879
I've been looking all over for you.

00:15:59.879 --> 00:16:00.879
Congratulations. You found me.

00:16:00.879 --> 00:16:01.879
Found me.

00:16:01.879 --> 00:16:03.879
Is this the part where you give me a stern talking to?

00:16:03.879 --> 00:16:05.879
You're looking for the crystal, aren't you?

00:16:05.879 --> 00:16:07.879
That's my business, not yours.

00:16:07.879 --> 00:16:10.879
You nearly took out an airplane, Kara.

00:16:10.879 --> 00:16:13.879
Do you have any idea how many people you could have killed?

00:16:13.879 --> 00:16:20.269
My mind kind of wandered.

00:16:20.269 --> 00:16:25.269
If you continue this way, it's only a matter of time before you get hurt, or found out.

00:16:25.269 --> 00:16:27.269
Why do you care?

00:16:27.269 --> 00:16:30.269
You're my cousin, Kara. I care about you.

00:16:30.269 --> 00:16:32.269
Well, family believes in one another.

00:16:32.269 --> 00:16:34.269
And you betrayed me.

00:16:34.269 --> 00:16:35.269
You'd rather talk to everyone.

00:16:35.269 --> 00:16:36.269
anyone else but me.

00:16:36.269 --> 00:16:39.269
I'm really trying here, but everything I've been told...

00:16:39.269 --> 00:16:40.269
By who?

00:16:40.269 --> 00:16:41.269
Your friend?

00:16:41.269 --> 00:16:42.269
The Martian Manhunter?

00:16:42.269 --> 00:16:45.269
My father wasn't a traitor.

00:16:45.269 --> 00:16:47.269
He didn't try to kill anyone.

00:16:47.269 --> 00:16:51.669
He was a good man.

00:16:51.669 --> 00:16:53.669
I'm going to prove that to you.

00:16:53.669 --> 00:16:55.669
Forget about the crystal could be anywhere.

00:16:55.669 --> 00:16:59.669
That crystal is the only thing I have left from home.

00:16:59.669 --> 00:17:00.669
But you could care less.

00:17:00.669 --> 00:17:01.669
That's not true.

00:17:01.669 --> 00:17:03.669
It's always about what you want.

00:17:03.669 --> 00:17:05.670
You act like such a hero.

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:06.670
But really?

00:17:06.670 --> 00:17:07.670
All you have really?

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:08.670
think about as yourself.

00:17:08.670 --> 00:17:11.670
I'm not the one who took off and didn't tell anybody where I went.

00:17:11.670 --> 00:17:14.670
Was I supposed to give you an itinerary?

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.670
We may be cousins.

00:17:16.670 --> 00:17:18.670
I don't have to like you.

00:17:18.670 --> 00:17:23.259
Stay out of my life.

00:17:23.259 --> 00:17:25.259
Not letting you leave.

00:17:25.259 --> 00:17:27.259
You don't have a choice.

00:17:27.259 --> 00:17:54.950
Kara?

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:58.950
You're okay. When'd you get back from D.C.?

00:17:58.950 --> 00:18:00.950
I just flew in.

00:18:00.950 --> 00:18:03.950
You know, Clark was looking for you. He was really worried.

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:05.950
Remember thinking about diving into the digital age.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:07.950
into the digital age. Use your cell phone.

00:18:07.950 --> 00:18:09.950
Don't worry about Clark.

00:18:09.950 --> 00:18:11.950
Look, I hope you don't mind me using your computer.

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.950
I just thought I'd check some stuff against the planet database.

00:18:14.950 --> 00:18:16.950
No, no, that's no problem at all.

00:18:16.950 --> 00:18:19.950
Feel free to rev your search engine here anytime.

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:22.950
Well, unless you're hacking into national security networks.

00:18:22.950 --> 00:18:30.109
Which is exactly what you're doing?

00:18:30.109 --> 00:18:34.109
Carrow, this is top secret information.

00:18:34.109 --> 00:18:37.109
They can trace my IP address and arrest me for this.

00:18:37.109 --> 00:18:39.109
No, not after running it through a Tor Park filter

00:18:39.109 --> 00:18:40.109
and rerouting it through half of us.

00:18:40.109 --> 00:18:41.109
and servers.

00:18:41.109 --> 00:18:44.420
You were a very mysterious girl.

00:18:44.420 --> 00:18:49.049
I'm trying to find who entered this one lab.

00:18:49.049 --> 00:18:51.049
Someone who could have stolen something from it.

00:18:51.049 --> 00:19:00.230
Have you ever heard of LX Dynamics?

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:02.230
Yeah, they're a Luther Corp Defense Contractor.

00:19:02.230 --> 00:19:05.230
We can assign it down on one of their plants.

00:19:05.230 --> 00:19:07.230
As in Lex Luthor.

00:19:07.230 --> 00:19:13.980
Here, uh, scoot over and I will pull up our file on them.

00:19:13.980 --> 00:19:21.740
And here...

00:19:21.740 --> 00:19:25.849
It is.

00:19:25.849 --> 00:20:38.150
Karat?

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:41.150
When I saw how that media rock disabled your ship,

00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:44.150
I figured I might do the same thing to the passenger.

00:20:44.150 --> 00:20:47.150
Tell you, boss, I only want what's mine.

00:20:47.150 --> 00:20:50.150
My boss is the United States of America.

00:20:50.150 --> 00:20:52.150
We have some questions for you.

00:20:52.150 --> 00:20:54.150
What the hell are you doing?

00:20:54.150 --> 00:20:56.150
Step back, Mr. Luther.

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:58.150
This is a matter of national security.

00:20:58.150 --> 00:21:00.150
I said, stand down.

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.150
You better have official authorization to make an arrest.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:03.150
You're being recorded.

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:04.150
I disabled the feed.

00:21:04.150 --> 00:21:06.150
My guards will be here in seconds.

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:08.150
I disabled them, too.

00:21:08.150 --> 00:21:09.650
What have you done to her?

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:10.650
I know that you stole something.

00:21:10.650 --> 00:21:11.650
something for me.

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:12.650
I don't know what you mean.

00:21:12.650 --> 00:21:15.650
Is it a coincidence that you were in my lab the same day she broke in?

00:21:15.650 --> 00:21:18.650
What makes you think she would break in your lab?

00:21:18.650 --> 00:21:22.650
I know you've got my property hidden somewhere in here, but it doesn't matter anymore.

00:21:22.650 --> 00:21:24.650
She's the real prize now.

00:21:24.650 --> 00:21:33.779
So blinded by devotion, he couldn't see the danger that you pose our planet.

00:21:33.779 --> 00:22:05.319
Clark, it's Lana.

00:22:05.319 --> 00:22:06.319
I know where Kara is.

00:22:06.319 --> 00:22:12.059
I don't need a frank assessment, Senator.

00:22:12.059 --> 00:22:15.059
Just your assurance, Agent Carter will be fired by morning.

00:22:15.059 --> 00:22:16.059
Where's Kara?

00:22:16.059 --> 00:22:18.059
Take it easy, Clark.

00:22:18.059 --> 00:22:20.059
Where is she?

00:22:20.059 --> 00:22:24.059
She was just arrested by the Department of Domestic Security.

00:22:24.059 --> 00:22:25.059
I swear to God likes if you lie.

00:22:25.059 --> 00:22:28.059
I tried to stop the agent, but he got the upper hand.

00:22:28.059 --> 00:22:30.059
I only want to help her.

00:22:30.059 --> 00:22:31.059
I wish I could believe you.

00:22:31.059 --> 00:22:32.059
I swear!

00:22:32.059 --> 00:22:34.059
She's been taken to a lab in Virginia.

00:22:34.059 --> 00:22:37.059
Clark, why would they arrest her?

00:22:37.059 --> 00:22:54.059
You're hurting me.

00:22:54.059 --> 00:22:56.059
Well, if I wasn't hurting you, you'd be hurting me.

00:22:56.059 --> 00:22:59.059
We humans, we call it survival of the fittest.

00:22:59.059 --> 00:23:00.059
I am human.

00:23:00.059 --> 00:23:01.059
Then how did you smash?

00:23:01.059 --> 00:23:04.059
How did you smash into an impenetrable vault?

00:23:04.059 --> 00:23:06.059
See, I talked to that lab tech

00:23:06.059 --> 00:23:08.059
when you tried to seduce?

00:23:08.059 --> 00:23:10.059
I know it was you.

00:23:10.059 --> 00:23:13.059
This machine will reveal the truth.

00:23:13.059 --> 00:23:15.059
Summer Holtz created this technology

00:23:15.059 --> 00:23:18.059
to force people to relive their memories,

00:23:18.059 --> 00:23:19.059
but it was unstable.

00:23:19.059 --> 00:23:22.059
Now I can control the process

00:23:22.059 --> 00:23:25.059
by delivering the Meteor Rock solution

00:23:25.059 --> 00:23:27.059
directly into your veins.

00:23:27.059 --> 00:23:30.059
I want to know about your home planet.

00:23:30.059 --> 00:23:31.059
You're a great.

00:23:31.059 --> 00:23:33.059
on it. It's called Earth.

00:23:33.059 --> 00:23:42.230
At the beginning.

00:23:42.230 --> 00:23:43.230
Where are you from?

00:23:43.230 --> 00:23:45.230
And when did you first arrive on this planet?

00:23:45.230 --> 00:23:46.230
Kara?

00:23:46.230 --> 00:23:53.130
You followed me?

00:23:53.130 --> 00:23:56.130
Well, with the speed we have on this planet, it wasn't hard.

00:23:56.130 --> 00:23:58.130
Visiting me at home is one thing, Kara,

00:23:58.130 --> 00:24:01.130
but sneaking through the last remaining portal

00:24:01.130 --> 00:24:03.130
to follow me here was far too dangerous.

00:24:03.130 --> 00:24:05.130
I had to get out of Kandor.

00:24:05.130 --> 00:24:09.130
The war's been getting worse, and I can hear the mines being bombed day and night.

00:24:09.130 --> 00:24:11.130
Does Zorel know you're here?

00:24:11.130 --> 00:24:12.130
You know, my father never lets me out of Kandor.

00:24:12.130 --> 00:24:15.130
My father never lets me out of Kandor alone.

00:24:15.130 --> 00:24:17.130
But he's been spending so much time in the lab,

00:24:17.130 --> 00:24:22.069
it's easy to sneak away.

00:24:22.069 --> 00:24:29.990
Why are you here?

00:24:29.990 --> 00:24:32.990
I wanted to see where my son may grow up.

00:24:32.990 --> 00:24:34.990
What, but you don't have...

00:24:34.990 --> 00:24:46.950
For you, I know how much you and Jarrell wanted this.

00:24:46.950 --> 00:24:48.950
He's our miracle baby.

00:24:48.950 --> 00:24:51.950
I don't understand. I mean, why would he grow up here?

00:24:51.950 --> 00:24:53.950
Kara...

00:24:53.950 --> 00:24:56.950
Krypton may never see the end of this war.

00:24:56.950 --> 00:24:58.950
Jorel's brain interactive construct

00:24:58.950 --> 00:24:59.950
may very well save us,

00:24:59.950 --> 00:25:03.950
but I won't risk my son's life on that chance.

00:25:03.950 --> 00:25:07.950
Well, I'll be there, and I'll protect him.

00:25:07.950 --> 00:25:12.950
As much as this pains me, it may be my only choice.

00:25:12.950 --> 00:25:19.619
I can't let the destiny of my child be dictated by the fate of a planet.

00:25:19.619 --> 00:25:24.309
And aren't you worried about your son growing up with humans?

00:25:24.309 --> 00:25:27.309
I mean, they're so primitive.

00:25:27.309 --> 00:25:31.309
Joral visited Earth many years ago, and he chose this family

00:25:31.309 --> 00:25:33.309
because he was impressed by their capacity.

00:25:33.309 --> 00:25:36.309
I hope it's more impressive than the way that they live.

00:25:36.309 --> 00:25:38.309
This place is a mess.

00:25:38.309 --> 00:25:40.309
It's one of many structures, Carrie.

00:25:40.309 --> 00:25:42.309
It's not the residents.

00:25:42.309 --> 00:25:43.309
Come, let me show you.

00:25:43.309 --> 00:25:44.309
Okay, Laura.

00:25:44.309 --> 00:25:50.250
You were here before the first meteor shower.

00:25:50.250 --> 00:25:52.250
No, I'm hallucinating.

00:25:52.250 --> 00:25:54.250
No, it wasn't an hallucination.

00:25:54.250 --> 00:25:56.250
You came to Earth in 1986.

00:25:56.250 --> 00:25:57.250
It's not true. I never...

00:25:57.250 --> 00:25:58.250
Where'd you visit?

00:25:58.250 --> 00:26:00.250
I didn't, I swear.

00:26:00.250 --> 00:26:01.250
That would be a lie.

00:26:01.250 --> 00:26:07.420
So, I guess we could use a little higher concentration.

00:26:07.420 --> 00:26:12.259
I want you to go back to your first journey.

00:26:12.259 --> 00:26:14.259
Go back to your first journey here.

00:26:14.259 --> 00:26:15.259
Who did you contact?

00:26:15.259 --> 00:26:19.339
I don't think they caught, Lara.

00:26:19.339 --> 00:26:21.339
Are these people here right now?

00:26:21.339 --> 00:26:22.339
No.

00:26:22.339 --> 00:26:25.339
They're attending a spiritual celebration called church.

00:26:25.339 --> 00:26:27.339
It's one of their traditions.

00:26:27.339 --> 00:26:33.059
It sure smells a lot better in here.

00:26:33.059 --> 00:26:35.059
They believe they're cooking.

00:26:35.059 --> 00:26:44.329
Sunday roast.

00:26:44.329 --> 00:26:48.329
It is so peaceful here compared to Krypton.

00:26:48.329 --> 00:26:50.329
It's a true home.

00:26:50.329 --> 00:26:52.329
I don't know.

00:26:52.329 --> 00:26:53.329
It's kind of...

00:26:53.329 --> 00:26:54.329
small.

00:26:54.329 --> 00:26:55.329
Cluttered.

00:26:55.329 --> 00:27:01.509
Careful, Kara.

00:27:01.509 --> 00:27:04.509
You must leave no trace of our visit.

00:27:04.509 --> 00:27:07.509
I don't want to influence them in any way.

00:27:07.509 --> 00:27:10.509
They're destined to raise my child.

00:27:10.509 --> 00:27:12.509
It's important they feel secure.

00:27:12.509 --> 00:27:15.509
Have you given your baby a name yet?

00:27:15.509 --> 00:27:17.509
No.

00:27:17.509 --> 00:27:21.509
With everything happening on Krypton, Jerell and I have yet to discuss one.

00:27:21.509 --> 00:27:26.099
He'll be so far from home.

00:27:26.099 --> 00:27:31.279
Our son will be nothing but a distant star.

00:27:31.279 --> 00:27:36.160
Maybe you could name him Kelle.

00:27:36.160 --> 00:27:40.160
And that way, when he looks at the sky, he can think of us.

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:42.160
Kallel.

00:27:42.160 --> 00:27:45.160
Well, that's a beautiful name.

00:27:45.160 --> 00:28:00.019
This must be her.

00:28:00.019 --> 00:28:01.019
She'll make a good mother.

00:28:01.019 --> 00:28:03.910
Para.

00:28:03.910 --> 00:28:05.910
Don't you want your son to have a picture of you?

00:28:05.910 --> 00:28:24.809
Zorrell!

00:28:24.809 --> 00:28:33.140
Get away from her!

00:28:33.140 --> 00:28:39.329
Oh my God.

00:28:39.329 --> 00:28:51.819
You don't one of them.

00:28:51.819 --> 00:28:52.819
I figured there was more of you.

00:28:52.819 --> 00:28:54.819
Living among us hiding in plain sight.

00:28:54.819 --> 00:28:56.819
She's been exposed too long.

00:28:56.819 --> 00:28:57.819
You're killing her.

00:28:57.819 --> 00:28:59.819
Extreme measures for extreme times.

00:28:59.819 --> 00:29:03.819
I had to push her to her limit to learn about your dangerous species.

00:29:03.819 --> 00:29:06.819
If you disconnect her, I'll tell you everything you need to know.

00:29:06.819 --> 00:29:08.819
Yeah, you will. When I'm done with her.

00:29:08.819 --> 00:29:11.819
Kera, wake up.

00:29:11.819 --> 00:29:28.470
Kara, you told you not to leave Kandor.

00:29:28.470 --> 00:29:33.470
It's my fault. I thought Kara could learn something about the world by coming here.

00:29:33.470 --> 00:29:34.470
It's not true.

00:29:34.470 --> 00:29:36.470
Kara. We'll wait outside.

00:29:36.470 --> 00:29:39.819
There's no reason to be angry.

00:29:39.819 --> 00:29:41.819
You know Kara is safe with me.

00:29:41.819 --> 00:29:42.819
Me?

00:29:42.819 --> 00:29:45.819
You always did watch out for her.

00:29:45.819 --> 00:29:47.819
In fact, I'm relieved you're here.

00:29:47.819 --> 00:29:51.819
We both know our planet could be destroyed soon.

00:29:51.819 --> 00:29:54.819
With the end so near, there's no reason to return.

00:29:54.819 --> 00:29:59.380
Stay with me here on Earth.

00:29:59.380 --> 00:30:02.380
We could rule this planet with strength as a family.

00:30:02.380 --> 00:30:03.380
No.

00:30:03.380 --> 00:30:05.380
Jorel is my husband.

00:30:05.380 --> 00:30:07.380
We're having a child.

00:30:07.380 --> 00:30:10.529
A son.

00:30:10.529 --> 00:30:19.640
Well, blood runs too cold to be a father.

00:30:19.640 --> 00:30:20.640
You tried to kill him.

00:30:20.640 --> 00:30:21.640
Why don't you try to kill him?

00:30:21.640 --> 00:30:22.640
What does that make you?

00:30:22.640 --> 00:30:23.640
Passionate!

00:30:23.640 --> 00:30:25.640
My brother stole you from me.

00:30:25.640 --> 00:30:26.640
He took away my life.

00:30:26.640 --> 00:30:28.640
Joril didn't steal me.

00:30:28.640 --> 00:30:31.640
But he'll never feel the way I feel about you.

00:30:31.640 --> 00:30:34.640
I know you love Kara.

00:30:34.640 --> 00:30:36.640
I'll love your son as my own.

00:30:36.640 --> 00:30:37.640
Zorrel, stop.

00:30:37.640 --> 00:30:38.640
You're delusional.

00:30:38.640 --> 00:30:41.640
We will be together, Laura.

00:30:41.640 --> 00:30:44.640
If not here today, then one day through my science.

00:30:44.640 --> 00:30:51.339
Your science?

00:30:51.339 --> 00:30:53.339
You stole my DNA?

00:30:53.339 --> 00:30:56.319
Your strands are safely stored within a

00:30:56.339 --> 00:31:01.339
crystal that like you is full of light and beauty.

00:31:01.339 --> 00:31:03.339
I refuse to be your next science experiment.

00:31:03.339 --> 00:31:06.339
Oh, you're much more than that, Laura.

00:31:06.339 --> 00:31:10.819
Father, how could you?

00:31:10.819 --> 00:31:13.819
I told you to wait outside.

00:31:13.819 --> 00:31:15.819
Oh, what are you doing? Stop!

00:31:15.819 --> 00:31:16.819
No!

00:31:16.819 --> 00:31:20.819
You will forget everything about this day.

00:31:20.819 --> 00:31:27.930
Kara!

00:31:27.930 --> 00:31:28.930
Kara!

00:31:28.930 --> 00:31:40.900
Come back.

00:31:40.900 --> 00:31:44.630
I'm sorry, Clark.

00:31:44.630 --> 00:31:45.630
I'd never told you about this place if I'd known how this place

00:31:45.630 --> 00:31:47.630
place if I'd known how dangerous it was.

00:31:47.630 --> 00:32:09.700
I'm so sorry.

00:32:09.700 --> 00:32:11.700
It's okay.

00:32:11.700 --> 00:32:13.700
Everything's gonna be all right.

00:32:13.700 --> 00:32:40.980
I don't believe it. After all this time...

00:32:40.980 --> 00:32:49.799
That means that I really was here.

00:32:49.799 --> 00:32:54.619
Everything that I saw is true.

00:32:54.619 --> 00:32:57.619
When I saw my mother in your memory, she was so beautiful.

00:32:57.619 --> 00:33:00.619
This is beautiful as she is in this picture.

00:33:00.619 --> 00:33:06.240
You really loved her, didn't you?

00:33:06.240 --> 00:33:08.240
I did.

00:33:08.240 --> 00:33:12.940
Just like I love my father.

00:33:12.940 --> 00:33:13.940
Until now.

00:33:13.940 --> 00:33:15.940
I thought he was such a god.

00:33:15.940 --> 00:33:21.589
A real Kryptonian hero.

00:33:21.589 --> 00:33:23.589
Sure right.

00:33:23.589 --> 00:33:27.829
He was nothing like that.

00:33:27.829 --> 00:33:30.829
Your father did some terrible things.

00:33:30.829 --> 00:33:33.829
But in his own misguided way, I'm sure he loved you.

00:33:33.829 --> 00:33:41.180
I don't know what's worse.

00:33:41.180 --> 00:33:45.180
Finding out the truth or losing who I thought he was.

00:33:45.180 --> 00:33:54.480
We're not defined by our parents, Kara.

00:33:54.480 --> 00:33:58.480
One of the most important things that my adoptive parents taught me

00:33:58.480 --> 00:34:00.480
is that we shape our own destiny.

00:34:00.480 --> 00:34:06.460
Maybe it's time I stopped holding on so tightly to my past

00:34:06.460 --> 00:34:10.460
and started looking ahead to my life on Earth.

00:34:10.460 --> 00:34:13.460
Find the kind of friends that you have.

00:34:13.460 --> 00:34:15.460
I'm sorry, Clark.

00:34:15.460 --> 00:34:17.460
I was so obsessed with trying to find the crystal

00:34:17.460 --> 00:34:19.460
that I put us both in danger.

00:34:19.460 --> 00:34:23.460
I don't blame you for wanting to find the crystal so badly.

00:34:23.460 --> 00:34:24.460
Especially now.

00:34:24.460 --> 00:34:26.460
I know how important it is.

00:34:26.460 --> 00:34:29.460
I said some terrible things to you.

00:34:29.460 --> 00:34:32.460
Things that weren't true.

00:34:32.460 --> 00:34:37.420
I'm happy.

00:34:37.420 --> 00:34:38.420
in my life, Clark.

00:34:38.420 --> 00:34:42.889
I'm happy to be in your life, Kara.

00:34:42.889 --> 00:34:49.820
Laura loved you very much.

00:34:49.820 --> 00:34:56.239
I'm glad you got to see my memory of her.

00:34:56.239 --> 00:34:57.239
Me too.

00:34:57.239 --> 00:35:02.820
I hope I can see her again someday.

00:35:02.820 --> 00:35:21.090
Striving for complete isolation?

00:35:21.090 --> 00:35:23.090
Dangerous choice.

00:35:23.090 --> 00:35:26.090
No man is an island entire of itself.

00:35:26.090 --> 00:35:30.090
Glad to know your son still ranks a spot on your busy itinerary.

00:35:30.090 --> 00:35:33.090
You know, I tried to use a Luther Corp jet the other night,

00:35:33.090 --> 00:35:35.090
but you'd already taken it to Washington.

00:35:35.090 --> 00:35:37.090
I'm amazed you'd be traveling so so.

00:35:37.090 --> 00:35:39.090
soon after your recent ordeal in the woods.

00:35:39.090 --> 00:35:41.090
I've got some catching out to do.

00:35:41.090 --> 00:35:47.090
Oh, I just, I've got a bit of news from my contacts at the Department of Domestic Security.

00:35:47.090 --> 00:35:55.010
There's a new girl in town, and apparently you are fascinated with her.

00:35:55.010 --> 00:36:01.659
If you're referring to Kara, Kent, I'm afraid you're mistaken.

00:36:01.659 --> 00:36:04.659
She just works for me at the town.

00:36:04.659 --> 00:36:09.659
First, Lana, now Kara, don't you think it's time to give up this fixation with Clark

00:36:09.659 --> 00:36:11.659
and everyone connected with him?

00:36:11.659 --> 00:36:13.659
So that's it?

00:36:13.659 --> 00:36:15.659
Your fatherly advice for the day?

00:36:15.659 --> 00:36:18.659
Can I take an interest in my son's well-being?

00:36:18.659 --> 00:36:20.659
Oh, and which son is that?

00:36:20.659 --> 00:36:23.659
You spend as much time protecting Clark as you do pushing me away.

00:36:23.659 --> 00:36:26.659
Exactly whose father are you?

00:36:26.659 --> 00:36:31.840
I wish I could say yours and be proud.

00:36:31.840 --> 00:36:33.840
Your treatment of Lana...

00:36:33.840 --> 00:36:34.840
Come on, Dad.

00:36:34.840 --> 00:36:36.840
I learned from watching you with Mom.

00:36:36.840 --> 00:36:41.340
I was just...

00:36:41.340 --> 00:36:43.340
Being a Luther.

00:36:43.340 --> 00:36:49.369
I don't know what you're being.

00:36:49.369 --> 00:36:50.369
You have crossed a Luther.

00:36:50.369 --> 00:36:57.369
line. Look, I realize your first instinct is to assume the worst, Dad.

00:36:57.369 --> 00:37:02.369
But believe me, I'm not that person anymore.

00:37:02.369 --> 00:37:07.369
You're right. You're not. These illicit projects of yours, you hide them like an expert.

00:37:07.369 --> 00:37:14.210
I'm sure you can fool the people around you. You can probably fool yourself.

00:37:14.210 --> 00:37:40.260
I think I owe you an apology for running off last night.

00:37:40.260 --> 00:37:43.260
I know what it's like to chase lead, Kara.

00:37:43.260 --> 00:37:45.260
I just hate to think that you only want me from my computer.

00:37:45.260 --> 00:37:46.260
from my computer.

00:37:46.260 --> 00:37:49.260
No, it just takes a lot to put a frown on that face of yours, James.

00:37:49.260 --> 00:37:54.260
And I was so focused on tracking down spaceships that I wasn't much of a friend.

00:37:54.260 --> 00:37:56.260
You were there for me every time.

00:37:56.260 --> 00:38:02.309
Don't you noticed?

00:38:02.309 --> 00:38:05.309
Noticed if it weren't for you, I wouldn't have had any leads to chase.

00:38:05.309 --> 00:38:08.690
Well, I don't know.

00:38:08.690 --> 00:38:11.690
Kara, I saw how fast he went from computers 101 to hack in the Pentagon.

00:38:11.690 --> 00:38:17.760
I think he can do just about anything once you put your mind to it.

00:38:17.760 --> 00:38:23.219
But right now, all I want to do is treat you to lunch.

00:38:23.219 --> 00:38:25.219
How about some more Chinese?

00:38:25.219 --> 00:38:26.219
I'm getting a hang of that whole chopstick thing.

00:38:26.219 --> 00:38:28.219
that whole chopstick thing.

00:38:28.219 --> 00:38:30.219
I'll go get my jacket.

00:38:30.219 --> 00:38:31.219
Okay, great.

00:38:31.219 --> 00:38:46.400
You're looking chipper?

00:38:46.400 --> 00:38:48.400
Really? I do?

00:38:48.400 --> 00:38:53.400
It's nothing. It's just, uh, beautiful day.

00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:57.900
You know, even though we're not each other's automatic plus one anymore,

00:38:57.900 --> 00:38:59.900
doesn't mean we still can't be friends.

00:38:59.900 --> 00:39:02.900
Are you doing anything for lunch?

00:39:02.900 --> 00:39:04.900
Actually, I have plans.

00:39:04.900 --> 00:39:10.260
With Kara?

00:39:10.260 --> 00:39:19.750
It's just lunch, Chloe.

00:39:19.750 --> 00:39:22.730
Look, I know how this is going to sound coming from me, but you and

00:39:22.750 --> 00:39:24.750
Kara from different worlds.

00:39:24.750 --> 00:39:26.750
Just be careful, okay?

00:39:26.750 --> 00:39:30.130
Chloe Kara's from Minnesota.

00:39:30.130 --> 00:39:56.670
It's not like she's from another planet.

00:39:56.670 --> 00:39:58.670
So, what's the big surprise?

00:39:58.670 --> 00:40:00.670
I wouldn't have found Kara if it wasn't for you.

00:40:00.670 --> 00:40:02.670
I'm glad you still have those contacts in the mansion.

00:40:02.670 --> 00:40:04.670
I'm just glad she's okay.

00:40:04.670 --> 00:40:07.670
Well, when I found her, Lana, she gave me this.

00:40:07.670 --> 00:40:16.519
Her name is Laura.

00:40:16.519 --> 00:40:23.619
She's stunning. Clark, this was taken in your house.

00:40:23.619 --> 00:40:24.619
When did you...

00:40:24.619 --> 00:40:27.619
It's a long story, Lana, but there is more.

00:40:27.619 --> 00:40:31.619
I told you I wanted to share everything with you.

00:40:31.619 --> 00:40:40.619
What's in that?

00:40:40.619 --> 00:40:54.960
Inside this crystal is my mother's DNA.

